    "source": "",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A heavy hauberk woven through with a fine tension-thread of reactive yesodium-doped wire, cut and rivetted by a journeyman armorer in one of the older Bad Eden plate-houses. The weave snags incoming force a half-beat before it lands, redistributing it into the wearer's stance instead of their ribs. Heavy. Expensive. Worth it.</p><p><strong>Reactive Lacing.</strong> While worn, the wearer may shift one die of incoming kinetic damage into Stress instead of Integrity, once per scene. No upkeep, no harmonization — the thread does the thinking.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    }
  },
